  "what_this_proves": "the complete W8A8 path works on the FPGA: int8 embedding gather with per-token rescale, per-token activation quantisation, int8 matmul on the AME with int32 accumulation, and dequantisation with the row and column scales in the contract's order. The cache position advances 16..23 and every step's logits match the reference, so the KV cache is genuinely being written and read across steps rather than a fixed shape being replayed.",
  "bugs_fixed_this_round": [
    {
      "symptom": "the extra cache-position argument, fixed in the previous round, had a twin: the prefill+decode image could not link",
      "cause": "each graph lowerer emits its own dealloc_helper, so two entry points compiled separately collide",
      "fix": "llvm-objcopy --redefine-sym on the decode object, the same treatment the FP32 image builder already used"
    },
    {
      "symptom": "the decode prototype was computed but never emitted",
      "cause": "the prelude was assembled from `prototype` only",
      "fix": "emit dec_prototype alongside it"
    }
